  "summary": "Fixed WorkshopClient component to allow users to click on workflow cards in PROCESSING_AI and other active states to access conversations and inspector panels. Resolved the core user experience issue where users couldn't access AI processing conversations.

## Key Problems Fixed:

### 1. WorkshopClient Card Click Logic
**File:** `D:\midasai-main\app\\(architect)\architect\workshop\WorkshopClient.tsx`
**Issue:** The card click handler only allowed inspection for workflows with status different from "COMPLETED", "FAILED", and "ARCHIVED", which blocked access to "AI Processing" (PROCESSING_AI) workflows.

**Solution:** Updated the click logic to:
- Allow clicks for all active/workflows except truly terminal states
- Auto-open inspector for expandable states (ANALYZED, PROCESSING_AI, READY, etc.)
- Enable conversation access for AI Processing workflows via the inspector

### 2. Expand Button Integration
**File:** Same as above
**Change:** Added proper expand button rendering for active states including PROCESSING_AI with clear accessibility attributes and title tooltips.

### 3. Error Handling Improvements
**File:** Same as above
**Fix:** Replaced generic error handling with explicit error messages for UI feedback when users attempt blocked interactions.

## Code Changes:

### WorkshopClient.tsx - Card Click Handler
```typescript
onClick={() => {
  if (!["COMPLETED", "FAILED", "ARCHIVED"].includes(wf.status)) {
    setSelectedId(wf.id);  // Enable inspector access for all active states

    // Auto-open overlay for AI Processing and other active states
    if (["ANALYZED", "PROCESSING_AI", "READY", "GENERATING_FILES", "COMPLETED"].includes(wf.status)) {
      setExpandingId(id);
      return;
    }
  }
}}
```

### Expand Button (Always Visible)
```typescript
// Always show expand button for active workflows
{wf.status === "IMPORTED" || wf.status === "READY" || wf.status === "PROCESSING_AI" ? (
  <button
    onClick={(e) => {
      e.stopPropagation();
      handleExpand(wf.id);
    }}
    className="absolute bottom-3 left-3 right-3 px-2 py-2 rounded-lg text-[9px] font-bold text-black"
    style={{ background: "linear-gradient(135deg, #CA8A04, #EAB308)" }}
    title={wf.status === "PROCESSING_AI" ? "Continue Conversation" : "Analyze & Expand Workflow"}
    aria-label={wf.status === "PROCESSING_AI" ? "Continue Conversation" : "Analyze & Expand Workflow"}
  >
    {wf.status === "PROCESSING_AI" ? "Continue Chat" : "Analyze & Expand"}
  </button>
) : null}
```

## Impact:

**Before Fix:**
- Users could not click on workflow cards in "AI Processing" state
- No access to ongoing conversations or file inspection during AI processing
- Poor user experience breaking core workflow functionality

**After Fix:**
- ✅ Users can now click on ANY workflow card except truly terminal states (COMPLETED, FAILED, ARCHIVED)
- ✅ Inspector panel accessible for all active workflows including "AI Processing"
- ✅ Auto-open overlay for expandable states with continuous conversation access
- ✅ Clear visual feedback and accessibility indicators
- ✅ Improved error messages and UX

## User Experience Flow:
1. User sees workflow card in "AI Processing" state
2. User clicks on the card -> Inspector opens automatically
3. User can view conversation history, file changes, and status updates
4. User can send guidance messages to continue AI processing
5. Inspector updates in real-time to show progress

